e 20 does not apply — nothing is being\n  provisioned). The \"RHOAI Documentation\" team assignment is inferred; the\n  strategy provides no Impacted Teams table (see Health Warnings).\n- **Scope level.** Epic scope stays at the functional level of the strategy\n  (keyboard operability, focus retention in modals, indicator consistency).\n  Specific implementation techniques (focus-trap utilities, indicator styling\n  approach) are left to the implementing team.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n- **Missing strategy sections.** The strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no\n  Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then Acceptance Criteria, and no\n  Non-Functional Requirements section. The decomposition proceeded with\n  available information; team assignments were taken from architecture context\n  (Dashboard → RHOAI Dashboard) and inferred for Documentation.\n- **Scope trap (mild).** HLR-3 requires a *published* conformance statement\n  before customer renewal. Publication channels and review sign-off for a VPAT\n  are a human process gate outside the code work; the docs epic carries an\n  explicit technical-review AC, but the renewal deadline itself is a business\n  commitment, not an engineering AC.\n- **Out-of-scope boundary.** Screen-reader semantics beyond what the keyboard\n  fixes require and flows outside the four audited ones are explicitly out of\n  scope; acceptance criteria below are scoped to the four audited flows only.\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nNot applicable — no external dependency with uncertain timing. The single\ndependency (docs after code) is internal to the strategy.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":19447,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b494c5a6eeadbf8","agent_id":"a7bfafc6be005fb30","session_id":"5475345a-5695-4c0a-a45f-922c8c9f46be","uuid":"fbede04e-bca6-48f1-a5fc-82944bf84d69","timestamp":"2026-10-21T16:06:09.220Z","subagent_type":"genera