{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b7b499b77c5ee96","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9017\n3\tscore: 14\n4\tpass: true\n5\trecommendation: accept\n6\tissues: []\n7\terror: null\n8\t---\n9\t## Review Summary\n10\t\n11\tScore: 14/14 — pass\n12\tRecommendation: accept\n13\t\n14\t## Criterion Details\n15\t\n16\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n17\tAll three HLRs are fully mapped: HLR-1 and HLR-2 (both P1) to RHAISTRAT-9017-E001, HLR-3 (P2) to RHAISTRAT-9017-E002. The traceability matrix in the decomposition summary is present and matches each epic's own HLR Traceability section. Priority inheritance is correct: E001 (P1) carries the priority of the P0/P1 code work it enables, and E002's P2 is correctly derived via the docs-authoring priority exception (strategy priority Normal → P2), not flagged as a violation. No priority collapse — HLR-1 and HLR-2 are both P1 and constitute one logical change on the same UI surfaces; the bundling design decision is justified.\n18\t\n19\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n20\tThe DAG has a single edge, E001 → E002, justified by Rule 11 (docs-authoring blocked by all Implementations). Cross-check passes: the mermaid diagram (`E001 --> E002`, dependency → dependent, correct direction) matches E002's frontmatter `dependencies: [RHAISTRAT-9017-E001]` and E001's empty list. No cycles, no invalid edges, no konflux-onboarding or license-validation epics (so rules 7/8/10 parallelism constraints don't apply), no conditional branch files. Critical path length 2 fits the S-strategy heuristic (1-2). Content cross-check: E002's scope (VPAT claims reflecting implemented behavior) consumes E001's output, and the edge exists — no missing data/artifact dependency.\n21\t\n22\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n23\tThe two epics split cleanly along the component/team tuple: (Dashboard, RHOAI Dashboard) for the code remediation and (Documentation, RHOAI Documentation) for the conformance content. No epic spans multiple components or teams. E001's size is bounded by the audit report's enumerated defect list across four flows — plausibly within a sprint — and no epic shows multi-sprint scope. No scope duplication between siblings (code fixes vs. content authoring are disjoint work products). No work-product type mixing: E001 is code only, E002 is content only.\n24\t\n25\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n26\tBoth epics are typed Implementation, which is correct: E001 produces code changes; E002 produces published documentation artifacts (a docs-authoring implementation, not an investigation — no uncertainty exists to resolve since the audit enumerates the defects and the strategy has no open questions). E002's `implementation_type: docs-authoring` is the right routing for a content-process component with no architecture-context file. No Investigation epics exist, and correspondingly no `gated_by`/`gate_failure_impact` fields are set anywhere — consistent.\n27\t\n28\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n29\tBoth epics are Implementation type and carry `ai_signals` (9-signal rubric) with `investigation_signals: null` — type-appropriate. Signal values are consistent with the strategy content and the rationales in the ai-signals files: E001's `change_specificity: 1` (audit enumerates exact defects), `open_questions: 1` (strategy states none), `repo_access: 1` (public odh-dashboard repo per architecture context), `human_process_gates: 1` (VPAT review correctly attributed to the docs epic, not this one) are all justified. E002's `human_process_gates: -1` is well-supported by HLR-3's explicit technical-review requirement and the renewal-blocking customer commitment. Rationale tables match frontmatter values exactly. (Arithmetic/thresholds not checked per instructions.)\n30\t\n31\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n32\tE001 has seven testable Given/When/Then ACs — one per audited flow, focus-indicator consistency, audit-defect resolution/disposition, and a pointer-regression guard. E002 has four testable ACs including the rule-mandated technical-review-before-publication AC for docs-authoring and the publication outcome (the renewal-blocking deliverable). No replacement work, so no rollback/feature-flag AC required; no konflux chain, so no build-pipeline AC required. Neither epic body references sibling epics by draft ID — both use full flow/component names.\n33\t\n34\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n35\tAll strategy scope is accounted for: the four audited flows' keyboard operability and focus indicators (E001), and the VPAT/accessibility-statement update, review, and republication (E002). Out-of-scope boundaries (screen-reader semantics beyond keyboard fixes, non-audited flows) are explicitly restated in both epics' scope sections. The customer-renewal commitment from the problem statement is carried into E002's description and publication AC rather than silently dropped. The docs-authoring epic is present as required by the strategy's documentation deliverable. Strategy-level context (missing Impacted Teams/Dependencies/AC sections, the VPAT publication process gate, team inference) is transparently recorded in the decomposition's Health Warnings rather than dropped. No conditional branches exist or are needed — the strategy has no bounded-outcome uncertainty.\n36\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-828654e62c7f85d6","agent_id":"ae20348f9b7bd524e","session_id":"5475345a-5695-4c0a-a45f-922c8c9f46be","uuid":"9e013813-6858-47e1-a414-c5b455ad2059","timestamp":"2026-10-21T16:10:10.021Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b7b499b77c5ee96","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9017 decomposition"}
