{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b52d52694721dcee","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9017-E001\n3\ttitle: Dashboard keyboard accessibility remediation for audited core flows\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9017\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 0\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Dashboard keyboard accessibility remediation for audited core flows\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic remediates the keyboard accessibility defects identified by the\n34\taccessibility audit in the four core Dashboard flows: project creation,\n35\tworkbench spawn, model deployment, and pipeline run submission. It makes each\n36\tflow fully operable with keyboard alone and makes focus indicators consistent,\n37\tso that keyboard users can complete these flows without pointer input.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Fix the focus-loss defects in modals used by the four audited flows so that\n42\t  keyboard focus is retained and returned appropriately when modals open and\n43\t  close (no focus traps).\n44\t- Make all controls reachable in the four audited flows (no keyboard-unreachable\n45\t  controls).\n46\t- Apply consistent, visible focus indicators across the audited flows, in line\n47\t  with the Dashboard's existing UI conventions.\n48\t- Address the per-flow defect list enumerated in the accessibility audit\n49\t  report; the audit report is the authoritative defect inventory for this epic.\n50\t- Out of scope: screen-reader semantics beyond what the keyboard fixes require,\n51\t  and any flows outside the four audited ones.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- Given a keyboard-only user, When they navigate the project creation flow from\n56\t  entry to completion, Then every step is operable by keyboard alone with no\n57\t  focus traps and no unreachable controls.\n58\t- Given a keyboard-only user, When they navigate the workbench spawn flow from\n59\t  entry to completion, Then every step is operable by keyboard alone with no\n60\t  focus traps and no unreachable controls.\n61\t- Given a keyboard-only user, When they navigate the model deployment flow from\n62\t  entry to completion, Then every step is operable by keyboard alone with no\n63\t  focus traps and no unreachable controls.\n64\t- Given a keyboard-only user, When they navigate the pipeline run submission\n65\t  flow from entry to completion, Then every step is operable by keyboard alone\n66\t  with no focus traps and no unreachable controls.\n67\t- Given a keyboard user moving focus through controls in the audited flows,\n68\t  When an element receives focus, Then a visible focus indicator is shown,\n69\t  consistent in style across all four flows.\n70\t- Given the audit report's enumerated defects, When the fixes are complete,\n71\t  Then each enumerated defect is resolved or explicitly dispositioned.\n72\t- Given a pointer user, When the accessibility fixes are in place, Then\n73\t  pointer-based operation of the four flows continues to work without\n74\t  regression.\n75\t\n76\t## HLR Traceability\n77\t\n78\t- HLR-1 (P1): The four audited core flows are fully operable by keyboard, with\n79\t  no focus traps or unreachable controls — covered by the flow-operability\n80\t  acceptance criteria above.\n81\t- HLR-2 (P1): Visible focus indicators are consistent across the audited\n82\t  flows — covered by the focus-indicator consistency acceptance criterion above.\n83\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-828654e62c7f85d6","agent_id":"ae20348f9b7bd524e","session_id":"5475345a-5695-4c0a-a45f-922c8c9f46be","uuid":"b2770b8f-08ea-4510-973a-6b351962756d","timestamp":"2026-10-21T16:10:21.688Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b52d52694721dcee","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9017 decomposition"}
